volume-title": "sverweij/dependency-cruiser", "author": "Verweij", "year": "2024"}], "event": {"name": "2024 14th International Conference on Dependable Systems, Services and Technologies (DESSERT)", "location": "Athens, Greece", "start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 10, 11]]}, "end": {"date-parts": [[2024, 10, 13]]}}, "container-title": ["2024 14th International Conference on Dependable Systems, Services and Technologies (DESSERT)"], "link": [{"URL": "http://xplorestaging.ieee.org/ielx8/11122113/11122022/11122242.pdf?arnumber=11122242", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 8, 22]], "date-time": "2025-08-22T23:57:36Z", "timestamp": 1755907056000}, "score": 32.68348, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11122242/"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024, 10, 11]]}, "references-count": 23, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1109/dessert65323.2024.11122242", "published": {"date-parts": [[2024, 10, 11]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 11]], "date-time": "2026-08-11T17:38:53Z", "timestamp": 1786469933313, "version": "build-2736575974"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2010]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 8, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Structured credit instruments offer an insight into markets\u2019 perceptions of the extent of future credit defaults.  Claims of different seniorities incur losses only if defaults reach different magnitudes, so their relative value offers an insight into the likelihood of losses being of different severities.  This paper matches the traded values of structured credit products by modelling the defaults of the underlying credits and their interdependence.  It offers an improvement on the industry-standard \u2018Gaussian copula\u2019 model in its ability to capture the \u2018tail event\u2019 of multiple firms defaulting together.  This allows policymakers to draw better inference as to the likely scale of defaults implied by structured credit prices.  It offers an indication of the extent to which defaults are driven by systemic shocks to firms\u2019 balance sheets. It may also be of use to those who trade structured credit products and may offer an improvement in risk management.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.1719046", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2012, 1, 5]], "date-time": "2012-01-05T07:54:50Z", "timestamp": 1325750090000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Extracting Information from Structured Credit Markets"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"given": "Joseph", "family": "Noss", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "78", "reference": [{"key": "ref1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "first-page": "259", "DOI": "10.1007/978-0-8176-4545-8_14", "article-title": "A generic one-factor L\ufffdvy model for pricing synthetic CDOs", "author": "H Albrecher", "year": "2007", "journal-title": "Advances in Mathematical Finance"}, {"key": "ref2", "author": "Anderson", "year": "2001", "journal-title": "New estimates of the UK real and nominal yield curves"}, {"key": "ref3", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1017/cbo9780511809781", "author": "D Applebaum", "year": "2009", "journal-title": "Levy processes and stochastic calculus"}, {"key": "ref4", "first-page": "299", "article-title": "Probability distributions of future asset prices implied by option prices", "volume": "36", "author": "B Bahra", "year": "1996", "journal-title": "Bank of England Quarterly Bulletin"}, {"key": "ref5", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.77429", "author": "B Bahra", "year": "1997", "journal-title": "Implied risk-neutral probability density functions from option prices: theory and application"}, {"key": "ref6", "first-page": "98", "article-title": "Gamma process dyn